&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Introduction&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We exist to wow our customers. We know we’re doing the right thing when we hear our customers say, “How did I ever live without Coupang?” Born out of an obsession to make shopping, eating, and living easier than ever, we are collectively disrupting the multi-billion-dollar commerce industry from the ground up and establishing an unparalleled reputation for being leading and reliable force in South Korean commerce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are proud to have the best of both worlds — a startup culture with the resources of a large global public company. This fuels us to continue our growth and launch new services at the speed we have been since our inception. We are all entrepreneurs surrounded by opportunities to drive new initiatives and innovations. At our core, we are bold and ambitious people that like to get our hands dirty and make a hands-on impact. At Coupang, you will see yourself, your colleagues, your team, and the company grow every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our mission to build the future of commerce is real. We push the boundaries of what’s possible to solve problems and break traditional tradeoffs. Join Coupang now to create an epic experience in this always-on, high-tech, and hyper-connected world&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is responsible for overseeing construction projects for new logistics facilities owned or master-leased by Coupang, from planning through construction execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position leads design, engineering, scheduling, quality, and risk management activities while establishing technical standards and performance requirements that support Coupang&#39;s operational needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director will collaborate with stakeholders across all disciplines, including architecture, mechanical, electrical, telecommunications, and fire protection systems, to ensure successful project delivery aligned with quality, schedule, and budget objectives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead project management activities for new construction projects in Taiwan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage the Taiwan Global Construction Team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and collaborate with stakeholders across architectural, mechanical, electrical, telecommunications, and fire protection disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct site reviews and project feasibility assessments during early project stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and revise design documents, manage permitting processes, establish design standards, and support key decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct technical reviews and recommend alternative solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assess and analyze the impact of applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process standardization and develop/improve SOPs (Standard Operating Procedures) and SOWs (Statements of Work)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and manage project schedules, analyze causes of delays, and implement recovery plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and monitor project budgets while managing costs and design changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop, implement, and document construction standards during project execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage bidding, contracting, and payment administration for project partners, including CM firms, design consultants, engineering consultants, and contractors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify project stakeholders and facilitate effective collaboration and coordination across internal and external parties
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Architecture, Architectural Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 17 years of experience in construction management, including design and construction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing construction projects for logistics facilities, manufacturing plants, or similar building types&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in construction or real estate development project management with strong communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing teams within construction or real estate development organizations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong reporting and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel domestically and internationally as required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional proficiency in Korean is required, along with proficiency in either English or Mandarin Chinese (verbal and written)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience throughout the full lifecycle of large-scale projects, including planning, design, procurement, construction management, and project closeout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional certifications such as Registered Architect, Professional Engineer, Master Craftsman, Engineer, or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Mandarin Chinese or Taiwanese (verbal and written)&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
