&lt;p&gt;您的個人資料將依 Coupang 招募隱私權政策進行蒐集與管理：&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Introduction&lt;/strong&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Coupang is reimagining the shopping experience with the goal of wowing each customer from the instant they open the Coupang app to the moment an order is delivered to their door.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our services in Taiwan include “Rocket Delivery” which offers next-day delivery for a wide selection of items at affordable prices, “Rocket Overseas” which offers free international delivery on millions of best-selling products from Korea, the U.S., and beyond.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;We are looking for talents to help us lead Coupang’s expansion in Taiwan. This is an exceptional opportunity to become a part of Coupang’s growth in Taiwan and create a world where our customers wonder, “How did I ever live without Coupang?”&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&lt;strong&gt; Logistics Training Specialist (CLS)&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;drives front-line operational efficiency across Linehaul, Driver, and Sortation workstreams. Sitting at the intersection of instructional design and floor execution, this role translates logistics workflows into hands-on, scalable training programs. The specialist works directly on the warehouse floor and in the yard alongside front-line workers, site supervisors, and safety leads to deliver real-time coaching, refine training materials, and rapidly resolve operational performance gaps.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Capabilities &amp;amp; Scope&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Design &amp;amp; Development:&lt;/strong&gt; End-to-end creation of modular, blended learning assets (job aids, short videos, floor checklists, and ILT decks) tailored to transport and warehouse ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-the-Floor Execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct facilitation of onboarding, skill-building workshops, and train-the-trainer programs on the dock and in the yard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Problem-Solving:&lt;/strong&gt; Direct alignment with site leadership to diagnose friction points—such as sortation mis-scans, dock delays, or compliance issues—and deploy quick micro-learning fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Content Design &amp;amp; Development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, update, and maintain modular training content for &lt;strong&gt;Linehaul, Driver, and Sortation&lt;/strong&gt; workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop blended learning formats: quick-reference job aids, short video modules, hands-on floor checklists, and instructor-led training (ILT) decks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all driver and linehaul training materials align with current standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Training Delivery &amp;amp; Execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct hands-on onboarding sessions and recurring skill-building workshops for new and existing sortation associates, linehaul dispatchers, and drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Spend time directly on the warehouse floor and in the yard to facilitate training, observe workflows, and deliver coaching on the spot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate train-the-trainer programs for peer leads or floor champions to scale training reach across shifts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operational Alignment &amp;amp; Needs Analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with shift supervisors, fleet safety leads, and site managers to pinpoint operational friction (e.g., sortation mis-scans, driver safety incidents, dock delay times).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rapidly iterate existing training materials or deploy micro-learning solutions to address identified performance gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leveling/Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; 2–5 years of experience in instructional design, technical training, or operational training—specifically within &lt;strong&gt;transportation, warehousing, or logistics&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on Familiarity:&lt;/strong&gt; Understanding of sortation processes (scanning, cross-docking, conveyor systems), commercial driver compliance, and linehaul yard ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instructional Tools:&lt;/strong&gt; Proficiency with instructional design tools and standard LMS administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; Engagement:&lt;/strong&gt; Ability to build instant credibility with front-line workers, truck drivers, and site leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
