&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;DART(Detection and Response Team) is responsible for detecting and responding to cyber threats across Coupang, with the objective of minimizing the potential impact of cybersecurity incidents on the organization, and the team currently operates through DART KR and DART US and is expanding its global coverage with the establishment of DART TW.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;CSOC(The Cyber Security Operations Center) proactively prevents security incidents through established detection rules and response procedures. When a potential security incident is identified, DART analyzes the event to determine whether it is a true or false positive and assesses its potential impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;For confirmed incidents, DART identifies the root cause, implements containment and mitigation measures to prevent further damage, and collaborates with cross-functional stakeholders to develop and execute long-term preventive controls, reducing the likelihood of similar incidents recurring. In addition to incident response activities, DART conducts threat hunting by analyzing a wide range of logs and artifacts collected through the SIEM platform. This enables the team to identify and address threats that may have evaded existing detection mechanisms, further strengthening the organization&#39;s overall security posture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
