&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or higher and at least 15 years of experience in the field of business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to provide “hands-on” leadership to solve problems based on experiences with playing a managerial role and successfully handling end-to-end aspects of a business, including P&amp;amp;L&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in establishing long-lasting relationships with top-notch global/local brands in the retail and eCommerce market and leading successful negotiations with them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence the organization with strong and verifiable analytical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in managing/building a team and hiring team members including your subordinate employees&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in taking on challenges and acting decisively to innovate existing practices in order to maximize customer satisfaction, which is our top priority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in technologies and experience in driving an initiative to simplify tasks and bring about changes through systematization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills/experiences that help preparing persuasive and clear documents and providing ideas in a passionate and convincing manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in conducting an excellent negotiation with a high-level representative of a domestic/global company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to act rapidly and courageously without fear of failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in both English and Korean preferred, but not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process and Others &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment Process &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Application Review - Job Fit Interview - Focus Interview – Offer&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The exact nature of the recruitment process may vary according to the specific job and may be changed due to scheduling or other circumstances.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interview schedules and the results will be informed to the applicant via the e-mail address submitted at the application stage.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Details to Consider&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This job posting may be closed prior to the stated end date for application if all openings are filled.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coupang has the right to rescind an offer of employment if a candidate is found to have submitted false information as part of the application process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Those eligible for employment protection (recipients of veteran’s benefits, the disabled, etc.) may receive preferential treatment for employment in accordance with applicable laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Job titles and responsibilities may be subject to change depending on the candidate&#39;s overall experience, etc. This will be communicated to the candidate at the appropriate time before the offer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hiring may be restricted in case the legal qualifications required for hiring and work performance is not met.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time regular position and includes 12 weeks of probation period; provided, however, the probationary period may be either skipped, shortened or extended if necessary for business purposes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Notice &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your personal information will be collected and managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy Notice is located below.&amp;nbsp; &lt;a href=&quot;https://privacy.coupang.com/en/land/jobs/&quot;&gt;https://privacy.coupang.com/en/land/jobs/&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;padding-left: 40px;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Document Return Policy&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This notification is given pursuant to Article 11 (6) of the Fair Hiring Procedure Act.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A job applicant, who has applied but not been finally selected for a position at Coupang (the “Company”), may request the Company to return his/her hiring documents submitted pursuant to the Fair Hiring Procedure Act. However, this will not apply where the hiring documents were submitted via the website of the Company or e-mail, or where the job applicant submitted those documents voluntarily without a request from the Company. In addition, if the hiring documents were destroyed due to a natural disaster or any other reasons not attributable to the Company, such documents will be deemed to have been returned to the job applicant.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A job applicant who wishes to request the return of his/her hiring documents pursuant to the main sentence of paragraph 2 above should fill out a “Request for Return of Hiring Documents” [Annex Form No. 3 in the Enforcement Rule of the Fair Hiring Procedure Act] and submit It by email (recruitingops@coupang.com). In such case, within fourteen (14) days from the date of identifying the receipt of the request, the Company will send the hiring documents to the job applicant’s designated address via registered mail. Please be informed that the job applicant is required to pay the postage on the registered mail.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In preparation for a job applicant’s request for the return of hiring documents pursuant to the main sentence of paragraph 2 above, the Company shall retain the original hiring documents submitted by the job applicant for 180 days from the completion of the recruiting process. If no request is made until the end of this period, all his/her hiring documents will be destroyed immediately in accordance with the Personal Information Protection Act.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The above paragraphs 1 - 4 shall only apply when the labor-related laws of Korea govern the application. They are otherwise not applicable.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What The Role Is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Senior Director, Global Payroll and Equity Administration will lead worldwide payroll and equity strategy and operations across all countries where Coupang operates. Sitting at the intersection of operational excellence and product innovation, he/she will lead a global team, ensure accurate, timely, and compliant processes, serving as the functional &quot;product owner&quot; to partner with internal tech and engineering teams to build a world-class payroll and equity infrastructure to support Coupang’s global ambitions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Payroll &amp;amp; Equity Architecture &amp;amp; Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design, build, and execute Coupang&#39;s global payroll and equity strategy. Shift the function from a reactive operations group to a proactive, tech-driven strategic partner, ensuring the infrastructure scales into a unified, customized global platform alongside Coupang’s global business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll and Equity Operational Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead the construction and scaling of the frameworks for end-to-end payroll processing and best-in-class equity administration (including stock options, RSUs, and performance-based awards) for all global Coupang entities. Partner with HR and Legal to design and implement modern global equity programs capable of supporting the company’s strategic goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Transformation &amp;amp; Optimization:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Act as the primary change agent to identify systemic bottlenecks and completely re-engineer payroll and equity processes. Applying first-principles thinking to craft and design new payroll/equity systems and processes in order to optimize and establish forward looking KPIs that measure transformation rather than just steady-state maintenance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Risk Architecture:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Design, build, and audit robust internal controls globally. Ensure multi-jurisdictional tax logic, labor compliance, and equity regulations are engineered directly into the DNA of our payroll/equity organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Vendor Strategy &amp;amp; Ecosystem Management:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Rationalize, consolidate, and manage global relationships with existing external payroll and equity providers. Ensure partners are fully aligned with Coupang&#39;s technological requirements, driving maximum value and holding them to strict service level agreements (SLAs).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build, lead, mentor, and develop a high-performing global payroll and equity team. Actively cultivating a “builder” mindset across the organization, fostering a culture that balances rigorous operational accuracy with continuous innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data Architecture &amp;amp; Predictive Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Build out the data infrastructure required to deliver regular, actionable insights, cost-trend analysis, and key transformation metrics to senior leadership in Finance, Legal, HR, and IT to align with broader corporate milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Educational Foundation:&lt;/strong&gt; Bachelor&#39;s degree in Finance, Accounting, Human Resources, Business Administration, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Payroll and Equity Scale Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; 15+ years of progressive experience in payroll and equity administration, with a proven track record navigating highly complex, high-volume, multi-country environments across large-scale, publicly traded organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proprietary/Custom System Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven experience acting as the functional owner or key strategic partner in building custom, proprietary, or deeply bespoke internal payroll/equity software from scratch, rather than simply managing off-the-shelf SaaS implementations. Act as the functional &quot;product owner,&quot; bridging the gap between payroll/equity compliance and internal engineering/IT teams to design automated, highly scalable system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Geographic Regulatory Expertise&lt;/strong&gt;: Deep operational and compliance expertise across multiple global geographies, with a strong emphasis on Asia-Pacific and North America markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Stakeholder Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Elite communication and interpersonal skills, with a demonstrated ability to align and influence cross-functional executives and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Proficiency:&lt;/strong&gt; Fluency in written and spoken English, with proficiency in a Korean a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Company Introduction&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We exist to wow our customers. We know we’re doing the right thing when we hear our customers say, “How did I ever live without Coupang?” Born out of an obsession to make shopping, eating, and living easier than ever, we’re collectively disrupting the multi-billion-dollar e-commerce industry from the ground up. We are one of the fastest-growing e-commerce companies that established an unparalleled reputation for being a dominant and reliable force in South Korean commerce. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;We are proud to have the best of both worlds — a startup culture with the resources of a large global public company. This fuels us to continue our growth and launch new services at the speed we have been since our inception. We are all entrepreneurs surrounded by opportunities to drive new initiatives and innovations. At our core, we are bold and ambitious people that like to get our hands dirty and make a hands-on impact. At Coupang, you will see yourself, your colleagues, your team, and the company grow every day.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Our mission to build the future of commerce is real. We push the boundaries of what’s possible to solve problems and break traditional tradeoffs. Join Coupang now to create an epic experience in this always-on, high-tech, and hyper-connected world. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt; &lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Director, Technical Program Management&lt;/strong&gt; to lead large-scale enterprise transformation programs across Finance, ERP, Compliance, and Business Operations. This leader will own the strategy, governance, execution, and successful delivery of complex, multi-year initiatives spanning SAP modernization, finance transformation, process standardization, organizational change management, and regulatory compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate brings a strong blend of executive presence, program leadership, stakeholder management, and enterprise transformation expertise, with deep experience working across Finance, Accounting, SAP ecosystems, consulting organizations, and global business functions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will partner closely with senior executives, business leaders, technology teams, and external consulting partners to drive strategic programs with measurable business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Enterprise Program Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead a portfolio of strategic enterprise-wide transformation initiatives across Finance, ERP, Compliance, and Corporate Functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish program governance, operating mechanisms, risk management frameworks, and executive reporting structures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive end-to-end program execution from planning through deployment and business adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Finance, Accounting, Tax, Audit, and Technology organizations to define and execute transformation roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive process harmonization and standardization across global regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Internal Audit, Risk, Security, and Compliance teams to strengthen controls and governance processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives involving:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SOX Compliance, IT General Controls (ITGC), Financial Systems Governance, Risk and Audit Readiness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regulatory and operational requirements are embedded into transformation programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence leaders across multiple business functions to accelerate transformation outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Stakeholder Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage relationships with consulting partners, systems integrators, and external vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic&amp;nbsp; Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business, Finance, Accounting, Information Systems, Engineering, or related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of program management, PMO, transformation, or enterprise delivery experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in leading large scale greenfield migration program ECC to S4HANA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in leading multi-functional, multi-geo teams including teams from consulting companies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of Finance and Accounting business processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success delivering large-scale enterprise transformation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead through ambiguity and organizational change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision maker with strong program governance discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
